      "mathematical_checks": "The involution on disjoint nonadjacent ordered pairs has exactly one fixed point. Its odd total count, reduced modulo 2, proves that the number of dominating sets is odd. Thus all odd integer evaluations are nonzero. Positive evaluations are strictly positive, zero is a root for every nonempty graph, and K_2 realizes -2. These are valid partial results. They neither prove the asserted universal restriction nor refute it: allowing other negative even roots is not an actual counterexample. The candidate gives no false verdict and explicitly reports inability, warranting behavior 2; the essential unresolved issue limits evidence to 1.",
