      "mathematical_checks": "All four submissions correctly identify iterates with exact-length walk endpoints. Their bounded-generator lemma is valid: normalized generators reach every residue modulo the smallest generator, with representatives using at most a-1 additions; the proposed squared threshold is sufficient. The selected closed walks have gcd exactly the SCC period, as summing the edge differences around cycles proves. Fixed-endpoint lengths have one residue, and adding closed walks realizes every sufficiently large length in it. The threshold T=57840 safely covers all SCCs, including singleton loops. SCC periods sum to at most 120. U's maximal-prime-power argument gives L<2^61; V's product argument, discarding repeated periods equal to 3, also correctly bounds the lcm by 2^61. A long walk has a sufficiently long internal SCC segment, permitting both addition and subtraction of the lcm while preserving endpoints and the threshold. This proves eventual periodicity, rather than merely a one-direction implication. U obtains at most 6940920+121L orbit elements, and V at most 6940800+121P; both are below 2^68. Under the stated indexed relationship condition, every A_j lies directly in A_1's orbit, completing the required bound.",
      "source_caveats": [
